448	### (e) Memory: `src/mastra/memory.ts`
449	
450	```ts
451	import { Memory } from '@mastra/memory';
452	import { MongoDBStore, MongoDBVector } from '@mastra/mongodb';
453	import { ModelRouterEmbeddingModel } from '@mastra/core/llm';
454	const uri = process.env.MONGODB_URI!, dbName = process.env.MONGODB_DB ?? 'quorum';
455	export const memory = new Memory({
456	  storage: new MongoDBStore({ id: 'quorum-store', uri, dbName }),
457	  vector: new MongoDBVector({ id: 'quorum-vector', uri, dbName }),        // Atlas Vector Search
458	  embedder: new ModelRouterEmbeddingModel('google/gemini-embedding-001'), // 768-d, same key
459	  options: {
460	    lastMessages: 20,
461	    semanticRecall: { topK: 4, messageRange: 1, scope: 'resource' },      // all threads of this chat
462	  },
463	});
464	```
465	
466	`resource = chat:<chatId>`. Threads: `roster:<chatId>` (every `/me`), `plan:<chatId>:<date>` (drafting), `recap:<chatId>:<date>`. With `scope: 'resource'`, drafting next week's plan can recall a `/me` from weeks ago and last Sunday's recap. That is the Atlas evidence. Mastra creates the vector index itself, which uses 1 of M0's 3 indexes. Don't create others.
