833	## 2.6 Fallback paths per component
834	
835	| Component | Failure signal | Fallback (keep the category only if its primitive still runs) |
836	|---|---|---|
837	| **Gemma tool calls in Mastra** | Gate 1 <16/20, empty tool calls, or JSON errors | **Prefetch:** code calls `forecast()` + `places()` and puts the results in the prompt. `quorum-notools` + `structuredOutput` with `jsonPromptInjection`. Mastra still owns memory and the agent, but "tools" is now *code-run tools*. Say so in Mastra's paragraph. Alternative: a structured dispatch loop where `generate` returns `{tool, args} | {final}` via `structuredOutput`, code executes, and the loop runs ≤4 times |
838	| Gemma 31B slow or rate-limited | p50 >40 s or frequent 429 | `QUORUM_MODEL=google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it` (MoE, ~4B active: [Gemma 4 overview](https://ai.google.dev/gemma/docs/core)). Temporal retries 429s anyway |
839	| Structured output fails | `response.object` undefined/invalid | `errorStrategy: 'fallback'` with a code-built 2-option plan from the top 2 `places()` results, flagged `fallback: true` in events (and disclosed) |
840	| Semantic recall / embeddings | `gemini-embedding-001` errors, or vector index won't build on M0 | Try `@mastra/fastembed` locally (dims change, so rebuild the index). If it still fails, set `semanticRecall: false`. Atlas still = storage + roster + plans ("long-term memory for an agent" in the category text). Say Vector Search was cut |
841	| **Atlas** signup asks for a card / cluster blocked | — | Mastra `LibSQLStore` (file) on the laptop for memory, plus plan state in the same file. **Drop the MongoDB category.** The Render plan page then shows only data pushed via a route, kept in memory and lost on sleep (disclose this) |
842	| **Render** asks for a card / build fails | — | Run the Mastra server on the laptop (`mastra dev`). **Drop the Render category.** Demo = video. The Temporal story loses the cold start but keeps the crash-resume |
843	| Render 512 MB OOM | Render logs "Out of memory" | Only the Mastra server runs on Render, which should fit (⚠ untested). Drop `@mastra/fastembed` if added; keep `lastMessages` ≤20 |
844	| Render cold start doesn't produce a retry | Render holds the request during spin-up and answers within 25 s on attempt 1 | Keep the 25 s `AbortSignal.timeout`. A ~60 s wake ([Render Free](https://render.com/docs/free)) should exceed it and show attempts >1 (⚠ whether Render holds or rejects requests while waking is unverified). If attempt 1 succeeds anyway, report "absorbed with no retry, N ms" from `plans.events`. Don't shorten the timeout just to manufacture a retry |
845	| **Temporal** bundler/ESM trouble | Worker won't start | CommonJS for `src/temporal/` (samples-typescript pattern). Last resort: Python SDK for the worker only (big time cost; avoid) |
846	| Changing workflow code during a run | Non-determinism error in UI | Never edit `workflows.ts` after `real-run-start`. If you must, use `if (wf.patched('v2')) {…}`, or start a *new* workflow type for new runs. Activities and Render code can change freely |
847	| Laptop sleeps or reboots | Timers fire late | Durable but late. Restart the dev server (same `--db-filename`), worker and bot. Timers fire immediately on resume. Report the delay honestly; it's also proof of durability |
848	| Telegram API hiccup | `getUpdates` fails | The loop retries on the next iteration. Telegram keeps unconfirmed updates. Activities to Telegram retry 6× |
849	| Group's chat isn't Telegram | Friends refuse to install | Use the Discord bot alternative (free; needs `discord.js` gateway + `/poll`-style buttons). **+3 h.** Decide at Gate 0, not later |
850	| SerpApi | Card asked, quota hit, or no real effect on the plan | Remove `liveCheck` and the SerpApi category entirely |
851	| **Entire** | Hooks didn't capture or the push lacks checkpoints | `entire status`, `git ls-remote origin 'refs/entire/checkpoints/*'`, `git show-ref entire/checkpoints/v1`. Import past sessions ([docs](https://docs.entire.io/guides/sessions/import-past-agent-history.md)). If nothing is shareable, drop the category |
852	
853	## 2.7 The real group run and the Sunday outing
854	
855	**Choose the outing to make it happen:** 2–3 hours, ≤30 km, Sunday morning (default 06:30–10:30 local), low cost. Pick a park walk, a short trail or a viewpoint, not a summit. Quorum's options decide *which*, but your instructions keep them small.
856	
857	**Sat 10:00–11:30 UTC onboarding:** pin a message in the Telegram group. Use it to explain `/join`, `/me <one thing that limits you>` (examples: "no car", "knee hates long descents", "must be home by 11", "broke this month"), `/forget`, and that messages sent *to the bot* are processed by Google's Gemini API free tier ("Content used to improve our products") unless you run the local mode. Get explicit "ok" from each person, and permission for **first names + quotes + one group photo** in a public post.
858	
859	**Capture list.** Everything here is real and timestamped. Put it in `docs/evidence/`, scrubbing tokens and phone numbers.
860	
861	| # | What | When | Becomes in the post |
862	|---|---|---|---|
863	| 1 | `{{WE_SHOULD_COUNT}}` and `{{SINCE_DATE}}` from the old chat export, plus `{{OUTINGS_COUNT}}` (how many times you actually went) | Fri | Opening "minutes" block |
864	| 2 | Screenshot: the `/plan` reply with 2–3 options and their `shapedBy` lines | Sat 11:30 | What I Built |
865	| 3 | Screenshot: the poll with votes as they land, plus vote timestamps from the UI | Sat | Demo |
866	| 4 | Temporal UI: workflow list, **Timeline** view (timers spanning hours), **Pending Activities** during the cold start (attempt N, last failure), the `ActivityTaskStarted` event JSON with `attempt` | Sat 17:00, Sun 00:30 | Temporal paragraph |
867	| 5 | `plans.events` for the run (every attempt, with ms) | Sun | "The cold start, in numbers" table |
868	| 6 | The 06:00 reminder message (timestamp visible) and the rain fallback if it fired | Sun 01:00 UTC | Demo |
869	| 7 | Outing: departure, arrival and return times; one group photo (consented); one landscape photo; who came (`{{CAME_COUNT}}`/`{{GROUP_SIZE}}`) | Sun | Demo → "Sunday" |
870	| 8 | Two verbatim quotes. Ask: "What would've happened without the bot?" and "What did it get wrong?" (`{{WHAT_THEY_SAID_1}}`, `{{WHAT_THEY_SAID_2}}`) | Sun | Demo, closing |
871	| 9 | At least **one thing the agent got wrong** (`{{AGENT_MISTAKE}}`), with what you changed | Any | How I Built It (honest concession) |
872	| 10 | `{{TAPS_PER_PERSON}}`: count each friend's messages to the bot plus poll taps; take the median | Sun | What I Built |
873	| 11 | Retrieval: run `/plan <next weekend> 4` (start and cancel the workflow) or a guarded debug route that queries the vector store. Screenshot the recalled roster line and recap that shaped the new options | Sun 06:00 UTC | Atlas paragraph |
874	| 12 | Render dashboard events: "service suspended (idle)" / spin-up time | Sun | Render paragraph |
875	
876	**If it falls through (it's still a real run; write it honestly):**
877	- **No quorum by Sat 17:00 UTC:** the workflow posts "no quorum". Screenshot it. Then do a **smaller outing** with whoever said yes (even 2 people), run `/plan <date> 2` as a second workflow, and write: "Quorum said no. Two of us went anyway." The title changes (see §3 alternatives). Category evidence is intact: timers, signals and retries all ran.
878	- **Rain:** the fallback *is* the best possible story. Make sure the fallback message and the `fallback` phase are screenshotted.
879	- **Morning-of cancellations:** record who came and why others didn't (with consent), and run the recap anyway.
880	- **Nobody goes at all:** go alone on the planned route. In the post, separate "what the system did" (true, with evidence) from "what the group did" (nothing). The bonus asks you to "take it outside, use it, and tell us how it went" ([Challenge page](https://dev.to/challenges/hacktoberfest-week1-2026-10-05)). Telling honestly is the requirement, not success.
881	- **Kill switch fired (B1):** the walk with a parent replaces all of the above. The same capture list applies, minus the poll.
882	
883	## 2.8 Evidence pass (screenshots judges will look for)
884	
885	1. Temporal: one image with the workflow **Timeline**, cropped so the timer bars and their "7 h 30 m" labels are visible, and one image of **Pending Activities: Attempt 3 · Last failure: TimeoutError**.
886	2. `kill -9` sequence on a `/plan test` run: (a) the worker terminal showing `Killed`, (b) the UI showing the workflow still Running with the timer counting, (c) after restarting the worker **and** the dev server (`Ctrl-C`, then restart with the same `--db-filename`), a vote lands and the workflow moves to `locked`. This beats the field's existing crash demo ([grasscast](https://dev.to/jamesdivis/grasscast-a-should-i-go-outside-forecast-that-learns-your-taste-from-a-few-dozen-outings-jac)) by showing a timer that spans days and people.
887	3. Atlas: the Collections tab (`members`, `plans`, `recaps`, Mastra collections) and the Atlas Search tab with the vector index JSON (`type: vector`, `numDimensions: 768`, `similarity`).
888	4. Render: the service page with "Free", the URL, and a log line from the wake-up.
889	5. Entire: `entire checkpoint explain <commit that set POLL_CLOSE/05:30>` output (first 15 lines), and the GitHub branch view of `entire/checkpoints/v1`.
890	6. The Gemma comparison table from `npm run smoke` (3 model rows).
891	
892	## 2.9 Demo plan
893	
894	- **Live URL** (Render): `/` landing with the thesis line, a 90 s video and a link to the real plan page `/p/<planId>` (status timeline, attempt log, first names only). **`/try`**: judges enter 3–5 fake people with constraints, a city or lat/lon and a date. They get 2–3 options with `shapedBy`. Warn on the page and in the post: "Free Render sleeps; the first load takes ~1 minute. That's the same nap Temporal retries through."
895	- **What is not live after you publish:** the Telegram bot and Temporal worker run on your laptop. Say so. The video and screenshots cover them.
896	- **Backup video (≤90 s, voiceover, unlisted YouTube; record with OBS):**
897	  - 0–6 s: on-screen text "{{WE_SHOULD_COUNT}} 'we should's. {{OUTINGS_COUNT}} outings." Voice: "Plans don't die from disagreement. They die because nobody holds the clock."
898	  - 6–25 s: Telegram: `/plan` → three options with "shaped by Sara's knee" → poll taps.
899	  - 25–45 s: Temporal UI: timeline with hour-long timers; `kill -9` the worker and restart; a vote lands; locked.
900	  - 45–60 s: 05:30: Pending Activity attempt 3 while Render wakes → success → the 06:00 reminder.
901	  - 60–80 s: real photos from Sunday, with one quote on screen.
902	  - 80–90 s: plan page on Render, repo URL, the thesis line again.
903	
904	## 2.10 Things to skip even if tempting
905	
906	- A React front end for the group (−4 h; the group lives in the chat).
907	- A carpool or route optimiser (−3 h; a roster line is enough).
908	- Making the bot an admin "so it can read everything" (kills the privacy argument).
909	- Deploying Temporal on Render (512 MB, ephemeral disk, no free workers: it would lose the state that is the whole point).
910	- Building a second chat platform "just in case" (decide at Gate 0).
911	- Polishing `/try` beyond one form (judges spend under 2 minutes there).
912	- Sentry or Copilot "since it's free" (not your categories; dilutes the story).
913	
914	---
915	
916	# PART III — PERSUASION ENGINEERING
917	
918	This part applies `persuasion-playbook.md` to Quorum. One structural rule overrides the usual winner template: **do not write a first-person engineering diary.** The post is framed as the **minutes of the group's real weekend**. It uses "we" (the group) and "you" (the reader), and keeps "I" for build decisions only. That makes it distinct, and it suits StoryBrand: the *group* is the hero, Quorum is the guide, and you are the narrator, not the protagonist.
